max_parallel = 4. All nodes have tracker_binding=none so the ready source is local graph (self).

Recompute the ready-set yourself from the graph WITHOUT trusting schedule-graph.py: eligible iff status=active AND confirmation_status=confirmed AND evaluation_status=pass AND implementation_readiness.status=complete AND every transitively reachable depends_on node is done/closed AND not held by an active lease AND resource_scope not overlapping (path-component ancestor/equal) any active lease's scope (lease record scope ∪ leased node's resource_scope). Then check:
1. ready-set equals your recomputation (report any mismatch);
2. zero blocked/draft/unconfirmed/evaluation!=pass/readiness!=complete in ready-set;
3. feature and task batches are separate; no batch exceeds max_parallel; zero resource_scope overlap pairs inside any batch;
4. each task hint has suggested_branch == devgraph/<graph_node_id> and claim_command in public form `/dev-graph worktree claim <id> --branch devgraph/<id> --session-id <session>`, and branches/commands are unique;
5. lease double-claim: active leases have unique graph_node_id, and no recommended node is leased.
Return a compact JSON verdict: {"verdict":"PASS|FAIL","recomputed_ready_tasks":[...],"recomputed_ready_features":[...],"mismatches":[...],"batch_overlap_pairs":[...],"excluded":{id:reason},"branch_claim_unique":bool,"notes":[...]}.
